<title>AUSTRIA: VA Tech unit gets 1 bln ATS Egypt order.</title>
<headline>VA Tech unit gets 1 bln ATS Egypt order.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Voest-Alpine Industrieanlagenbau (VAI), a subsidiary of Austrian engineering group VA Tech, said on Tuesday it had received an order worth some one billion schillings to build a complete steelworks in Egypt.</p>
<p>The order comes from the privately-owned Egyptian firm Suez Steel Company, VAI said in a statement.</p>
<p>The mini mill plant with a capacity of 600,000 tonnes per annum will be located in Adabia, Suez Province and is scheduled to begin operating in 21 months time.</p>
<p>The production of billets will mainly feed the existing Egyptian rolling mills, VAI said. -- Vienna newsroom, +431 531 12256</p>
</text>
